# Upload Audio

> Uploads an audio file and returns a `file_id` for cloning. Files are scoped to the workspace.

`multipart/form-data`, field name `file`. Supported types: `audio/wav`, `audio/mpeg`, `audio/mp3`, `audio/mp4`, `audio/ogg`, `audio/webm`. Maximum 10 MB.

Clone sample requirements: 16-bit WAV / MP3 / M4A, sample rate ≥ 16 kHz, mono or stereo (first channel only). The sample must be **at most 15 seconds** of continuous clear speech. Very short clips (under roughly half a second) may fail because the service cannot transcribe them — aim for at least a few seconds.

> **Errors**
>
> Error responses use the same `{code, message, data}` envelope; a non-zero `code` identifies the error.
>
> | Case | Error code |
> | - | - |
> | Missing `file` field | `20010 missing file field` |
> | Empty file | `20006 empty file` |
> | Larger than 10MB | `20007 file too large` |
> | Unsupported audio type | `20008 unsupported media type` |
> | Invalid multipart form | `20009 invalid multipart form` |


